      <div type="clause" n="6">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Af">Af</ref> 6</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="6" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="52" ed="#liebermann"/>VII. Gif hwa on cirican<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#Af_6.lnote.oe.10"/> hwæt geðeofige, forgylde<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="37" target="#Af_6.lnote.oe.37"/> þæt angylde<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="38" target="#Af_6.lnote.oe.38"/>, ⁊ ðæt wite swa to ðam<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="39" target="#Af_6.lnote.oe.39"/> angylde<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="40" target="#Af_6.lnote.oe.40"/> belimpan<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="41" target="#Af_6.lnote.oe.41"/> wille, ⁊ slea mon þa hond<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="42" target="#Af_6.lnote.oe.42"/> óf ðe he hit mid gedyde.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="43" target="#Af_6.lnote.oe.43"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="6" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="52" ed="#liebermann"/>VII. Gif hwa on cirican<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Af_6.lnote.oe.6"/> hwæt geþeofige, forgylde ðæt angylde, ⁊ þæt wíte swa to þam angylde belimpan wille, ⁊ slea mon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Af_6.lnote.oe.3"/> þa hond<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Af_6.lnote.oe.3"/> of ðe he hit mid (stæl<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Af_6.lnote.oe.5"/>) dyde.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="6" corresp="#wit-b-no-prol"><pb n="53" ed="#liebermann"/>Bę ða<hi rend="italic">m</hi> ðe steleð on ciric<hi rend="italic">ean</hi>.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Af_6.lnote.oe.6-2"/> Gyf hwá on cyricean hwæt geþeofig<hi rend="italic">e</hi>, forgylde þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> angylde, ⁊ þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> wite swa to ðam angylde gelimpan wylle, ⁊<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="*" target="#Af_6.lnote.oe.star"/> slea mon ða hand óf, ðe he hit mid gedyde.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="6" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="53" ed="#liebermann"/>Si quis in ecclesia furetur aliquid, restituat<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="17" target="#Af_6.lnote.oe.17"/> hoc semel, et forisfactum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="18" target="#Af_6.lnote.oe.18"/>, sicut ad angildum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="19" target="#Af_6.lnote.oe.19"/> pertinet; et amputetur ei manus de qua furatus est.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="66–68" ed="#attenborough"/>[Be ðam ðe steleð on ciricean.] Gif hwa on cirican hwæt geðeofige, forgylde þæt angylde, ⁊ ðæt wite swa to ðam angylde belimpan<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#Af_6.attnote.fn.1"/> wille, ⁊<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#Af_6.attnote.fn.2"/> slea mon þa hond óf, ðe he hit mid [stæl]<ptr type="editorNote" n="3" target="#Af_6.attnote.fn.3"/> gedyde.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="7" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="300" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>{VII} Gif hwa on cirican hwæt geðeofige, forgylde þæt angylde, ⁊ ðæt wite swa to ðam angylde belimpan wille, ⁊ slea mon þa hond óf ðe he hit mid gedyde.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="53" ed="#liebermann"/>Wenn jemand in der Kirche<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_6.lnote.de.1"/> etwas stiehlt, vergelte er das mit einfachem Ersatz<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_6.lnote.de.2"/>; und das Strafgeld, wie<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Af_6.lnote.de.3"/> es zu jenem Ersatz gehören möge<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Af_6.lnote.de.4"/>; und schlage man die Hand ab, womit er es gethan<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Af_6.lnote.de.5"/> hat.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">If someone steals anything in a church, let him repay it with single compensation, and the fine as may belong to that compensation; and let the hand with which he did it be struck off.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="67" ed="#attenborough"/>If anyone steals anything from a church, he shall pay the value of the article and the fine which is appropriate to the value in question, and the hand shall be struck off which committed the theft.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="411" ed="#whitelock"/>If anyone steals anything in church, he is to pay the simple compensation and the fine normally belonging to that simple compensation, and the hand with which he did it is to be struck off.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="301" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>If someone steals something from a church, let him pay for it single-fold, and the fine such as is appropriate to the single-payment, and let the hand be struck off with which he did it.</ab>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#liebermann"><ref target="clause:IIAs_5">II As 5</ref></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="272"><label>cross-reference</label> <ref target="clause:Af_9-1">Af 9.1</ref> <quote>6, (ref. 9:1)</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="280"><label>revises (rights of the Church)</label> <ref target="clause:Ine_5">Ine 5–5.1</ref> <quote>theft from a church was additionally penalized (n. 79: Af 2 – 2:1, 5 – 5:4, 6 – 6:1; Ine 5 – 5:1, 6:1)</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="280"><label>revises (rights of the Church)</label> <ref target="clause:Ine_6-1">Ine 6.1</ref> <quote>theft from a church was additionally penalized (n. 79: Af 2 – 2:1, 5 – 5:4, 6 – 6:1; Ine 5 – 5:1, 6:1)</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="301"><label>compare</label> <ref target="clause:Ine_18">Ine 18</ref> <quote>Compare Ine §18 and §38, which similarly require the amputation of the offending hand.</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="301"><label>compare</label> <ref target="clause:Ine_37">Ine 37</ref> <quote>Compare Ine §18 and §38, which similarly require the amputation of the offending hand.</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="325"><ref target="clause:Af_32">Af 32</ref></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#whitelock" n="419"><ref target="clause:IIAs_5">II As 5</ref></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="148"><ref target="clause:IIAs_5">II As 5</ref></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_6.lnote.oe.10" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">52</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">þær <hi rend="italic">So</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">þær So</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_6.lnote.oe.37" n="37" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">52</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-gyld <hi rend="italic">So Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-gyld So Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_6.lnote.oe.38" n="38" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">52</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ung. <hi rend="italic">So</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ung. So</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_6.lnote.oe.39" n="39" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">52</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ðæm <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ðæm Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_6.lnote.oe.40" n="40" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">52</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-ld <hi rend="italic">So</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-ld So</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_6.lnote.oe.41" n="41" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">52</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-lym- <hi rend="italic">So Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-lym- So Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_6.lnote.oe.42" n="42" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">52</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">hand <hi rend="italic">So Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">hand So Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_6.lnote.oe.43" n="43" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">52</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">dyde <hi rend="italic">So</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">dyde So</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_6.lnote.oe.6" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">52</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Rasur vor</hi> an</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">erasure before an</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_6.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">52</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">o <hi rend="italic">geänd. in</hi> a</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">o altered to a</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_6.lnote.oe.5" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">52</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">übergeschr.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">written above</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_6.lnote.oe.17" n="17" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">53</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">et <hi rend="italic">fügt zu Hk T</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">et added by Hk T</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_6.lnote.oe.18" n="18" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">53</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">sit <hi rend="italic">fügt zu Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sit added by Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_6.lnote.oe.19" n="19" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">53</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">id <hi rend="italic">K</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">id K</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_6.lnote.oe.6-2" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">53</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">oder</hi> cirice <hi rend="italic">laut Af</hi> 8 <hi rend="italic">aufzulösen</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">or to be expanded as cirice, following Af 8</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_6.lnote.oe.star" n="*" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">53</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">æt oþrum cerre <hi rend="italic">am Rande, wohl im</hi> 12. <hi rend="italic">Jh., zugefügt;</hi> ⁊ <hi rend="italic">halb ausradirt.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">æt oþrum cerre added in the margin, probably in the 12th cent.; ⁊ half erased.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_6.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">52</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">‘Von dem der stiehlt in der Kirche’ Rb B. Wahrscheinlich diesen Satz zitiert II As 5. — <hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Kirchenraub 4. 5, zu trennen von Raub an Dritten, der nicht die Kirche materiell, nur den Kirchenfrieden (<hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 2a) schädigt</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">‘Of him who steals in the church’ Rb B. This sentence is probably quoted by II As 5. — <hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Kirchenraub 4. 5, to be distinguished from robbery of third parties, which does material damage not to the church but only to the peace of the church (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 2a)</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_6.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">53</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">‘das einfache Ersatzgeld’, also <hi rend="italic">angylde</hi> als ac. wie <hi rend="italic">u.</hi> 9, 1 zu verstehen, ist hier nicht nötig. — Die Busse (<hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 4. a) fällt fort, weil Leibesstrafe eintritt</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">It is not necessary here to understand ‘the single restitution payment’, i.e. to take <hi rend="italic">angylde</hi> as acc., as <hi rend="italic">below</hi> 9, 1. — The compensation (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 4. a) lapses because corporal punishment applies</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_6.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">53</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Das Verhältnis zwischen Ersatz und Strafe (<hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 14) erörtert Af 9, 1</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">The relation between restitution and penalty (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 14) is discussed in Af 9, 1</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_6.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">53</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">‘soll, pflegt’; <hi rend="italic">s. Wb willan</hi> 7. 8. 9</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">‘shall, is wont to’; <hi rend="italic">see Wb willan</hi> 7. 8. 9</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_6.lnote.de.5" n="5" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">53</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">‘stahl’ H cor; <hi rend="italic">vgl. Gl</hi> Hand 10. 11</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">‘stole’ H cor; <hi rend="italic">cf. Gl</hi> Hand 10. 11</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Af_6.attnote.fn.1" n="1" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">68</biblScope></bibl><label>belimpan</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">gelimpan</hi>. B.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Af_6.attnote.fn.2" n="2" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">68</biblScope></bibl><label>⁊</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">æt oþrum cerre</hi>, addition to B, probably in 12th century.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Af_6.attnote.fn.3" n="3" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">68</biblScope></bibl><label>stæl</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">(<hi rend="italic">stæl</hi>) <hi rend="italic">dyde</hi>. H*.</seg></note>
      </div>
